From: mscharged-port
Subject: Parse friend code digits into a writable buffer
Upstream-base: 9046e67aa2077a7eb4ed6e28c9df3c1d3b368f84
Classification: native compiler contract; no game behavior change.

SHOnlineFriendCodeEntry::ParseFriendKey converts each entered digit with
nlWcsToStr(mDigits[i], digit, 4) into digit, which pointed at the string
literal "0". CodeWarrior placed literals in writable memory; natively
they are in read-only .rodata, so confirming a friend code crashed in
nlWcsToStr with a write fault. The literal also had two bytes for a
four-byte maximum; only the two-character digit kept the copy short.

Natively the digit is converted into a four-byte local buffer, matching
the length passed to nlWcsToStr; nlWcsToStr always writes its first
character, so the buffer needs no initializer. atoi reads the same digit
as before. Console builds keep the original literal.

diff --git a/src/Game/SH/SHOnlineFriendCodeEntry.cpp b/src/Game/SH/SHOnlineFriendCodeEntry.cpp
index 0abb524..87a6d24 100644
--- a/src/Game/SH/SHOnlineFriendCodeEntry.cpp
+++ b/src/Game/SH/SHOnlineFriendCodeEntry.cpp
@@ -180,7 +180,11 @@ void SHOnlineFriendCodeEntry::SetSelectedDigit(int index)
 unsigned long long SHOnlineFriendCodeEntry::ParseFriendKey()
 {
     unsigned long long friendKey = 0;
+#if defined(MSCHARGED_NATIVE)
+    char digit[4];
+#else
     char* digit = "0";
+#endif
     for (int i = 0; i < 12; ++i)
     {
         nlWcsToStr(mDigits[i], digit, 4);
